{{!
    @template local_oksigeniaeguahe/panel_answer_path

    A path: how many got to each step, one family one mark. Full, they did; a ring, they did not; a small dot, it is not
    known. Under each step, what its marks are, each with its families. When there are too many families to see one by
    one (dots is false), the same as a bar.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * total - the families of the first step: every step is drawn on it
    * dots - whether each family is a mark
    * steps - name, n, url (its families, or nothing), parts (kind: yes, no or unknown; n), legend (kind, n, text, url) and
      haslegend

    Example context (json):
    {"total": 58, "dots": true, "steps": [{"name": "Vinieron", "n": 41, "url": "#",
        "parts": [{"kind": "yes", "n": 41}, {"kind": "no", "n": 5}, {"kind": "unknown", "n": 12}], "haslegend": true,
        "legend": [{"kind": "no", "n": 5, "text": "no vinieron", "url": "#"}]}]}
}}
<ol class="qs-camino{{^dots}} qs-camino-barra{{/dots}}" style="--total: {{total}}">
    {{#steps}}
    <li class="qs-paso">
        <span class="qs-paso-nombre">{{name}}</span>
        <span class="qs-paso-n">{{#url}}<a href="{{url}}">{{n}}</a>{{/url}}{{^url}}{{n}}{{/url}}</span>
        <span class="qs-pista" aria-hidden="true">{{#parts}}<i class="qs-tramo qs-{{kind}}" style="--n: {{n}}"></i>{{/parts}}</span>
        {{#haslegend}}<span class="qs-leyenda">{{#legend}}{{#url}}<a href="{{url}}">{{/url}}{{^url}}<span>{{/url}}{{#kind}}<i class="qs-marca qs-{{kind}}" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/kind}}{{#n}}<b>{{n}}</b> {{/n}}{{text}}{{#url}}</a>{{/url}}{{^url}}</span>{{/url}}{{/legend}}</span>{{/haslegend}}
    </li>
    {{/steps}}
</ol>
